            <div xml:id="d712">

                <pb facs="0768" n="758" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg758"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.515/4–1649: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-04-16">April 16,
                        1949</date>.<lb/>[Received April 16—9:27 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>776. Vernacular press today reports Control Yuan yesterday approved and sent to
                    Executive Yuan bill calling for Government to return hoard of gold, silver and
                    foreign currencies which last January was sent by Central Bank to Taiwan and
                    Amoy for safekeeping.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 776, repeated Embassy Canton 259, Shanghai 383.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
